// Hand-written gold dataset. 3 languages x 11 rows (8 answerable + 3
// must-refuse each). Every answerable row's source article was checked against
// the indexed chunks in data/chunks/<jurisdiction>/<number>/<lang>.jsonl.
// Questions and keywords remain human-maintained evaluation targets, not
// legal advice.
//
// Format: one JSON object per line. Fields: id, lang ("de"|"fr"|"it"),
// question, expected_sources (["<collection> <nr> Art. <x>", ...] -- federal
// e.g. "SR 220 Art. 335c", cantonal e.g. "sGS 811.1 Art. 2"), expected_keywords
// (2-4 terms in the question's language that a correct answer would
// contain), must_refuse (bool; true rows use empty expected_sources /
// expected_keywords and need no source verification).
//
// Federal rows above; cantonal rows below (SG/sGS, BE/BSG), added after the
// first real SG/BE ingest landed. Each cantonal row's source article was
// checked against the real indexed chunks in data/chunks/SG and
// data/chunks/BE (see corpus.yaml and docs/swiss-legal-rag.md for the
// cantonal pilot plan). Two rows (seed-sg-05, seed-be-05) cite a federal
// source alongside the cantonal one where the two genuinely co-govern
// (municipal autonomy, cantonal sovereignty).
